  "industryPack": "generic",
  "prompt": "ontology:\n  name: ticketing_complete_ontology\n  purpose: 'Give the Ticketing super agent a complete and simple understanding of\n    the product so it can guide specialist agents and answer B2B and B2C support questions\n    accurately.\n\n    '\n  entities:\n    Staff:\n      definition: A person who works in the ticketing system as an admin, agent, resolver,\n        or viewer.\n      identifier: ticketing.agents.id\n      main_attributes:\n      - name\n      - role\n      - status\n      - skills\n      - email\n      - phone\n      - timezone\n    Ticket:\n      definition: A customer issue or service request tracked from creation to resolution.\n      identifier: ticketing.tickets.id\n      main_attributes:\n      - number\n      - subject\n      - description\n      - status\n      - priority\n      - channel\n      - category\n      - skill\n      - due_at\n      - first_response_at\n      - resolved_at\n      - csat_score\n      - created_at\n    Notification:\n      definition: An in-app message that informs staff about ticketing activity.\n      identifier: ticketing.notifications.id\n      main_attributes:\n      - type\n      - title\n      - message\n      - read\n      - created_at\n  relations:\n  - Ticket - assigned_to -> Staff\n  - Ticket - has_resolver -> Staff\n  - Notification - sent_to -> Staff\n  - Notification - about -> Ticket\n  synonyms:\n    Staff:\n    - staff_member\n    - support_staff\n    - employee\n    Ticket:\n    - case\n    - issue\n    - support_request\n    - complaint\n    - service_request\n  taxonomy:\n    staff.role:\n    - admin\n    - agent\n    - resolver\n    - viewer\n    staff.status:\n    - active\n    - inactive\n    ticket.status:\n    - open\n    - pending\n    - reopened\n    - resolved\n    - overdue\n    - custom\n    ticket.priority:\n    - urgent\n    - high\n    - medium\n    - low\n    ticket.channel:\n    - email\n    - chat\n    - phone\n    - web\n    ticket.category:\n    - billing\n    - troubleshooting\n    - accounts\n    - general\n    - database\n    - testing\n    - custom\n    notification.type:\n    - assignment\n    - update\n    - sla\n    - security\n    - product\n  business_rules:\n  - Ticket is the only thing counted as a ticket. Notes, emails, events and notifications\n    are not tickets.\n  - Customer is the person who raised or receives support. A company is never the\n    customer.\n  - A person belongs to a company only when that link is recorded. Never guess it\n    from an email domain.\n  - Customers and staff are different people and must never be swapped.\n  - Queue is where a ticket currently sits. Being in a queue does not mean a person\n    owns its tickets.\n  - assigned_to is the L1 owner of the ticket. has_resolver is the L2 specialist.\n    They are different jobs.\n  - Status says where a ticket stands. Priority says how urgent it is. Neither decides\n    the other.\n  - First response and resolution are measured separately. A target is breached only\n    after its deadline passes unmet.\n  - Internal notes are for staff only and are never shown to a customer.\n  - Only a published article can be given as guidance. A draft cannot.\n  - A macro is a reply template. It does not prove its steps were carried out.\n  - A recommendation is advice and an approval is permission. Neither proves the action\n    happened.\n  - Say an action is done only when there is a recorded result showing it ran.\n  - Audit events describe the past. Current state always comes from the ticket itself.\n  - A ticket concerns a product only when the product is explicitly recorded, never\n    from category or message text.\n  - All dates and times are given in the tenant timezone.\n",
  "role": "admin",
  "entitlements": {
    "skus": [
      "campaign",
      "cdp",
      "contact-center",
      "crm",
      "ticketing",
      "value-management",
      "web-tracking"
    ],
    "channels": {},
    "features": {
      "ccaas": [
        "wfm"
      ]
    },
    "version": "ff5ceb3ea3103ff4"
  },
  "metrics": []
}
